# RECON-W30: the JMH result file from the run that exposed the --include filter bug.
# It holds 230 results from the whole jar while its own log claimed a filter was applied,
# so committing it would put a misleading measurement in the evidence directory. Kept
# locally only; docs-v2/operations/bench/README.md names it explicitly.
docs-v2/operations/bench/w30-perf-20261002-122937.json

# RECON-W31.4: the acquired Wikidata corpus (1 893 facts) is NOT committed. It is
# regenerable byte-for-byte from scripts/knowledge_forge/forge.py against a public
# endpoint, and pinning a snapshot of someone else's encyclopedia in this repo buys
# little. The two files that ARE force-added are the ones a result depends on:
# holdout.json (the evaluation contract) and acquisition-report.json (what was actually
# obtained, including the failures).

# RECON-W33.1: real BitNet checkpoint (1178.6 MB), provisioned by
# scripts/provision-bitnet.sh. Weights are downloaded, not committed.
data/models/bitnet-checkpoint/
data/models/**/*.safetensors
data/models/**/*.safetensors.sha256

# AI for OpenIDE — local agent state (chat transcripts, memory, snapshots; may contain secrets).
.aiforopenide/
!.aiforopenide/config.json

# RECON-W38.4: CUDA/ONNX native-library links are machine-local state. They were
# committed to git and pointed into one developer's untracked virtualenv and a
# single CUDA install, so a fresh clone had dangling links. scripts/diagnose-cuda.sh
# --repair recreates them locally; they are never committed.
.onnx_libs/

# Runtime artefacts at the repository root (added 2026-11-22). The jqwik property
# database and the API gateway's task store are MACHINE STATE, not content: the
# gateway's database is created by RemoteTaskStore ("data/mind/tasks.sqlite",
# relative to the working directory), and the root-level jqwik database is the
# same artefact the matrix-core one already excludes. Neither is ever committed.
# The owner's documents under OpeAi/ ARE committed - they are the programme's
# directive and handoff record, not machine state.
/.jqwik-database
/matrix-api-gateway/data/

# The PARALLEL SESSIONS' scratch directories (added 2026-11-24). A session keeps its
# working copies, its evaluator's evidence and its build output at the repository root,
# and those copies are MACHINE STATE: gigabytes of Gradle output and copies of the
# repository inside the repository. The four prefixes below are the sessions' naming
# convention and they name no real module (the modules are matrix-core, matrix-fpga,
# matrix-micro, matrix-operator, matrix-quality, matrix-ros2, matrix-spigot,
# matrix-tools-distill, matrix-web-ui, matrix-sdk-java, matrix-sdk-js, matrix-sdk-python,
# matrix-api-gateway, matrix-audit, matrix-billing, matrix-brain-runtime and
# matrix-observability). The documents' own evidence is RETAINED under
# docs-v2/engineering/evidence/, so nothing that matters is lost by ignoring the
# scratch itself. A NEW prefix must be added here.
/matrix-crj-*/
/matrix-dsh-*/
/matrix-revision-*/
/matrix-source-*/
